{
  "$comment": [
    "THREE DIFFERENT THINGS THAT ALL SOUND LIKE 'THIS DOCUMENT SUPPORTS THREE PARTIES'.",
    "",
    "D4.18's admission rule made party_3_name acceptable on 28 document types at once. That is a fact about",
    "the ENGINE, and on its own it says nothing about whether a promissory note should have three makers or",
    "whether anyone has checked. Collapsing the three levels below is how a structural capability turns into",
    "an implied legal claim, so they are recorded separately and asserted separately.",
    "",
    "  ADMITTED_BY_ENGINE          A third principal survives sanitisation, reaches the roster, and is named",
    "                              and bound in the artifact. Purely structural: it follows from the family",
    "                              declaring a principal series at 1 and 2, and nobody decided it per family.",
    "",
    "  EXPOSED_BY_INTAKE           The form actually offers a box for a third principal. Today NO family does:",
    "                              /document-config/:type builds fields from the schema, which declares two.",
    "                              The capability is reachable only by an API caller. This is not an oversight",
    "                              to correct — a form field is an invitation, and inviting a third principal",
    "                              into a document nobody has reviewed for three would be the product asserting",
    "                              readiness it does not have.",
    "",
    "  LEGALLY_SUPPORTED           An advocate has established that THIS family operates correctly with more",
    "                              than two principals: that the statute permits it, and that the clauses the",
    "                              family ships have been classified for N-party behaviour. NOT_REVIEWED for",
    "                              every family, because portfolio classification stands at 12.5%.",
    "",
    "THE RULE, WHICH IS THE POINT OF THE FILE:",
    "",
    "    ADMITTED_BY_ENGINE  =/=  EXPOSED_BY_INTAKE  =/=  LEGALLY_SUPPORTED",
    "",
    "Admission never implies exposure. Exposure must never be derived from admission — a family becoming",
    "technically capable of receiving party_3_name must not cause the UI to present that field as though the",
    "family had been reviewed. Exposure follows legal support, not the other way round.",
    "",
    "WHY THE PROMISSORY NOTE IS NOT A BUG TO FIX BY INTUITION. PROMISSORY_NOTE and POWER_OF_ATTORNEY are",
    "admitted by the engine and a third principal in either is doubtful. The temptation is to add an exclusion",
    "list. That would be guessing at law in a JSON file: whether a note can have three makers is a question",
    "under the Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881, and whether a power of attorney can have three donors is a",
    "question under the Powers-of-Attorney Act, 1882. Neither has been researched here, so both are recorded",
    "NOT_REVIEWED like the rest. An unreviewed family is not exposed to users, which is the containment."
  ],
